5af1-80a1-f8970be8eb8b" :question/math-academy-id "q-22979" :question/problem "Which of the following angles are coterminal with $\\theta =-{95}^{∘}?$\n\n- ${625}^{∘}$\n- ${160}^{∘}$\n- $-{455}^{∘}$" :question/worked-solution "To find the coterminal angles of a given angle $\\theta $, we add and subtract integer multiples of ${360}^{∘}:$\n\nLet's start by adding multiples of ${360}^{∘}$ to $-{95}^{∘}$:\n\n- $-{95}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}={265}^{∘}$\n\n- $-{95}^{∘}+2\\cdot {360}^{∘}={625}^{∘}\\,✓$\n\nOf the given values, there is no angle greater than ${625}^{∘}.$ So we can stop there.\n\nNow, let's subtract multiples of ${360}^{∘}$ from $-{95}^{∘}$\n\n- $-{95}^{∘}-{360}^{∘}=-{455}^{∘}\\,✓$\n\nOf the given angles, only ${625}^{∘}$ and $-{455}^{∘}$ are coterminal with $-{95}^{∘}.$\n\nSo the correct answer is I and III only." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-22979/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bba0ad98-6940-502a-873c-8a589a03a499"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-22979"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-22984/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "9c7fc5dc-1382-507a-bee9-299374e56b63" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-22984/selection/b1a9f2bb9f9bd59b66c906c9ab98446a26ec623744a7f92356bb121785f6cea5" :answer/id #uuid "71ea9b5e-2d12-5e12-8273-4c5575fd34b3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-22984/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "8b4469c6-d075-5d73-baad-25f557da8189" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-22984/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "f3700d87-3443-5005-9334-e439aa751883" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-22984/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "b6d8d0cf-f4a1-5fcb-9199-69656fc5b161" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-22984/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f379d197-7992-501b-88af-92f31e188315" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-22984/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-22984/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-22984/selection/b1a9f2bb9f9bd59b66c906c9ab98446a26ec623744a7f92356bb121785f6cea5" "q-22984/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-22984/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-22984/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-22984" :question/id #uuid "72a396d7-e8cf-5458-9d0a-c10ca03427ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-22984" :question/problem "Which of the following angles are coterminal with $\\theta =2\\pi $\n\n- $4\\pi $\n- $5\\pi $\n- $-2\\pi $" :question/worked-solution "To find the coterminal angles of a given angle $\\theta $, we add and subtract integer multiples of $2\\pi :$\n\nLet's start by adding multiples of $2\\pi $ to $2\\pi $:\n\n- $2\\pi +2\\pi =4\\pi \\,✓$\n\n- $2\\pi +2\\cdot (2\\pi )=6\\pi $\n\nOf the given values, there is no angle greater than $6\\pi .$ So, we can stop there.\n\nNow, let's subtract multiples of $2\\pi $ from $2\\pi $:\n\n- $2\\pi -2\\pi =0$\n\n- $2\\pi -2\\cdot (2\\pi )=-2\\pi \\,✓$\n\nOf the given angles, only $4\\pi $ and $-2\\pi $ are coterminal with $2\\pi .$\n\nSo the correct answer is I and III only." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-22984/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d65819f-0528-527e-8d1a-20421e221ca5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-22984"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-23191"] :question/problem "Which of the following angles are coterminal with $\\theta =-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}?$\n\n- $\\frac{4\\pi }{3}$\n- $\\frac{10\\pi }{3}$\n- $-\\frac{8\\pi }{3}$" :question/worked-solution "To find the coterminal angles of a given angle $\\theta $, we add and subtract integer multiples of $2\\pi :$\n\nLet's start by adding multiples of $2\\pi $ to $-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$:\n\n- $-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2\\pi =\\frac{4\\pi }{3}\\,✓$\n\n- $-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2\\cdot (2\\pi )=\\frac{10\\pi }{3}\\,✓$\n\nOf the given values, there is no angle greater than $\\frac{10\\pi }{3}.$ So, we can stop there.\n\nNow, let's subtract multiples of $2\\pi $ from $-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$:\n\n- $-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}-2\\pi =-\\frac{8\\pi }{3}\\,✓$\n\n- $-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}-2\\cdot (2\\pi )=-\\frac{14\\pi }{3}$\n\nOf the given angles, all three are coterminal with $-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.$\n\nSo the correct answer is I, II, and III." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-34403"] :question/problem "The angle $\\theta =-\\frac{9\\pi }{4}$ is represented in the coordinate plane in the usual way. In which quadrant does it lie?" :question/worked-solution "First, we find an angle that's coterminal with $-\\frac{9\\pi }{4}$ by *adding* integer multiples of $2\\pi $ until we get an angle that lies in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$\n\n- $-\\frac{9\\pi }{4}+2\\pi =-\\frac{\\pi }{4}$\n\n- $-\\frac{9\\pi }{4}+2\\cdot (2\\pi )=\\frac{7\\pi }{4}\\,✓$\n\nSo the angle $-\\frac{9\\pi }{4}$ is coterminal with $\\frac{7\\pi }{4}.$ Let's draw this coterminal angle in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977500/assets/891959642b0d055d852329c59be7541179dd5ae0c4182c2bec533261ce3a700d.png)\n\nWe see that $\\frac{7\\pi }{6}$ lies in quadrant IV. Therefore, $-\\frac{9\\pi }{4}$ also lies in this quadrant." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-124707/selection/cc54ccae9ecbe61a650173303111652be25e358bea2c6fc89973c699ac869f66" :answer/id #uuid "30e87dee-e647-52cd-9da8-56fc054e7e52" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124707/selection/4ca814a26a9344b418765bf1216091351959544cfa5933e8f718fbb4daf8fcd7" :answer/id #uuid "56e38090-95df-5db7-8495-6bea995248d8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124707/selection/950b08b6ce80f3e39ed6df93387e6b27d26252dee3574ece2f6ad977f5921545" :answer/id #uuid "66da0f38-31fa-5f51-8bd1-0b5e6a0fe3b1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "IV" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124707/selection/6cef23069c284027c89d195df9fea27427e9a7779aa03b92f69bdc30aa1481f3" :answer/id #uuid "f996bccc-b3d3-5796-bcf0-cb628bc10d4c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124707/selection/cad070e5505a4117987910fbb6a5b1c2cd8fd809933cb8aa2c675d22a4b3a3a9" :answer/id #uuid "aee4d362-b9eb-5fb6-99a1-bd156728dc9b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Between quadrants II and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124707/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3bcc09e5-bdca-52ca-a12b-94e93877a51f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124707/selection/6cef23069c284027c89d195df9fea27427e9a7779aa03b92f69bdc30aa1481f3" :answer-field/choices ["q-124707/selection/cc54ccae9ecbe61a650173303111652be25e358bea2c6fc89973c699ac869f66" "q-124707/selection/4ca814a26a9344b418765bf1216091351959544cfa5933e8f718fbb4daf8fcd7" "q-124707/selection/950b08b6ce80f3e39ed6df93387e6b27d26252dee3574ece2f6ad977f5921545" "q-124707/selection/6cef23069c284027c89d195df9fea27427e9a7779aa03b92f69bdc30aa1481f3" "q-124707/selection/cad070e5505a4117987910fbb6a5b1c2cd8fd809933cb8aa2c675d22a4b3a3a9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124707" :question/id #uuid "eaa1873e-b871-5487-ad2a-55300889eb98" :question/math-academy-id "q-124707" :question/problem "The angle $\\theta =-{530}^{∘}$ is represented in the coordinate plane in the usual way. In which quadrant does it lie?" :question/worked-solution "First, we find an angle that's coterminal with $-{530}^{∘}$ by *adding* integer multiples of ${360}^{∘}$ until we get an angle that lies in the range $[{0}^{∘},{360}^{∘}).$\n\n- $-{530}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}=-170$\n\n- $-{530}^{∘}+2\\cdot {360}^{∘}={190}^{∘}\\,✓$\n\nSo the angle ${190}^{∘}$ is coterminal with $-{530}^{∘}.$ Let's draw this coterminal angle in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977500/assets/1e741939f538fc5dfba9b5ff6f3b4ce0e68c5ebd746dfae533d3209c0c29feba.png)\n\nWe see that ${190}^{∘}$ lies in quadrant III. Therefore, $-{530}^{∘}$ also lies in this quadrant." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-124707/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "993c8fe4-dae9-5dc4-9f94-5012f905e0ee"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124707"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
